# Harness

`harness/` scores open-core Favlo pipelines only. A cloud-only pipeline's agent lives in the sibling cloud tree's `custom-harness/`. Do not add a harness here that names or imports a cloud pipeline.

## Pipeline-agnostic media agents

A media agent that calls one generate tool does not hardcode a pipeline id, a published tool name, or a pipeline package import. It takes `--pipeline` and one or more `--tool` local names. Those names are what the pipeline already publishes. The agent builds `{pipeline}__{tool}` with `harness.mcp_media.published_name` and registers exactly those names on a Microsoft Agent Framework `MCPStreamableHTTPTool` (`allowed_tools`). The smoke body comes from `docs/<pipeline>/smoke.json` (or another card path the command documents). Quality and folder defaults stay with the host when the note omits them.

Wrong: `wan22_i2v__generate_video` in source, `docs/ace-step-15-turbo/smoke.json` with no `--pipeline`, or `from z_image_turbo…` inside a harness.

Right:

```text
python -m harness.image_smoke_agent --pipeline <id> --tool generate_image
python -m harness.video_smoke_agent --pipeline <id> --tool generate_video
```

## Exceptions

- Language, coding, needle, synthetic, and benchmark harnesses take `--model` (the language pipeline id). They are not media MCP generate agents.
- `harness.media_pipeline` discovers registered media pipelines and their published tools from the catalog. It does not take `--pipeline` / `--tool` for one folder.
- Helpers (`mcp_media`, `inspect_wav`, `server`, …) are not end-to-end scores.

## Docs

A harness CLI change updates [docs/harness.md](../../docs/harness.md) in the same change. Pipeline notes that quote the command pass the same `--pipeline` and `--tool` flags.
